---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import CuteLayoutGemm from "../../component/Cute/CuteLayoutGemm.astro";
---

<Layout title="CuteLayoutGemm demo">
	<h1>CuteLayoutGemm demo</h1>

	<h2>Copy and multiply, UniversalFMA</h2>
	<p>
		A scaled-down version of a 128×128×8 CTA tile with 256 threads (a 32×8 copy layout and a 16×16 MMA layout):
		32×16 matrices, a 16×16×4 CTA tile and 32 threads, laid out 8×4 for both the copy and the MMA. Stage 1
		copies one k tile of A or B into shared memory; stage 2 multiplies the shared tiles into each thread's
		accumulators. Edit any layout or index, hover an element to find it in the other columns, click a cell to
		switch thread.
	</p>
	<CuteLayoutGemm block={[1, 0]} thread={5} kTile={1} />

	<h2>K-major B with a row-major copy layout</h2>
	<p>
		mB is K-major (stride 1 along K), so tB = (8,4):(4,1) puts consecutive threads along K, where the global
		addresses are contiguous. sB stays N-major. Copy stage only.
	</p>
	<CuteLayoutGemm stages="copy" operand="B" bMatrix="(32,16):(16,1)" bThr="(8,4):(4,1)" block={[0, 1]} thread={5} />

	<h2>Ampere tensor core: SM80_16x8x8_F32F16F16F32_TN, 2×1 warps</h2>
	<p>
		Two warps, each issuing mma.m16n8k8, with K-major (TN) shared tiles. Thread 5 is lane 5 of warp 0: it holds
		A(1,2), A(1,3), A(9,2), A(9,3), as in the PTX fragment tables. MMA stage only.
	</p>
	<CuteLayoutGemm
		stages="mma"
		atom="SM80_16x8x8_F32F16F16F32_TN"
		mmaThr="(2,1)"
		cta="(32,16,8)"
		aSmem="(32,8):(8,1)"
		bSmem="(16,8):(8,1)"
		gC="(32,16)"
		thread={5}
	/>
</Layout>
